An empty-clears rule sends an empty slice as [], so the peer clears the collection,
and omits a nil one, which leaves it unchanged; a property no rule names omits
both. protocol.json states the rule, which ACP's table holds for its own
definitions only (0049-MADR-remediate-the-2026-11-01-debugging-pass.md, G35).

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {"Opts": {"type": "object", "properties": {"tags": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "Replace the tags. An empty array clears them."}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}}}, "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}}}
-- protocol.json --
{"EmptyClears": [{"Definition": "Opts", "Property": "tags", "Source": "An empty array clears them."}]}
